+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   **Perspective Divide Non-Linearity:** The projection is non-linear. The affine approximation is valid only locally around the centroid. For very large Gaussians or extreme FOV, this approximation may introduce geometric warping artifacts [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Singular Covariance:** If the determinant of the 2D covariance is zero or negative, the inverse is undefined. This can happen if the Gaussian is viewed edge-on or if numerical errors accumulate. Stabilization ($\epsilon_{2d}$) mitigates this [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Depth Sorting:** Gaussians must be sorted by depth ($z_c$) before compositing to ensure correct alpha blending [S7, unofficial].
+*   **Aliasing:** Without stabilization, small Gaussians can cause high-frequency aliasing. The low-pass filter ensures minimum pixel coverage [S5, unofficial].
